If you want to parameter‑tune a guidance law (e.g., find the optimal navigation constant N), you can construct a family of functions with different constants using functools.partial before passing them to CustomLibrary.
from functools import partial
pn_N4   = partial(mg.pn_basic, N=4.0)
pn_N5   = partial(mg.pn_basic, N=5.0)
pn_N6   = partial(mg.pn_basic, N=6.0)
# add them to the library list
all_funcs.extend([pn_N4, pn_N5, pn_N6])
When SINDy runs, the coefficients attached to pn_N4, pn_N5, pn_N6 will tell you which navigation constant best explains the data.
 
